# Netlify redirects.
#
# The live site ranks on these URLs. A 301 passes that ranking to the new
# address; without it the old page 404s and the ranking is lost, which is the
# most common way a rebuild silently costs traffic.
#
# Keep every path the old site published, even ones that look obsolete.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GlamifiedHR is now the homepage (see `productOnHome` in site.config.js).
#
# The "!" is a force flag: without it Netlify serves a file that exists at the
# path in preference to the rule, and /products/ and /products/glamified-hr/
# are still built — the engine builds them for multi-product variants. Forcing
# the redirect is what makes them unreachable, so the product has exactly one
# URL. Remove these two lines the day a second product goes back on the site.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/products                 /                            301!
/products/*               /                            301!

# The old product URLs. HR goes to its page, which is now the homepage.
/glamifiedhr              /                            301
/glamified-hr             /                            301
/hr                       /                            301
/payroll                  /                            301

# GlamifiedSales and GlamifiedFleet are no longer sold from this site. They go
# to the homepage rather than 404ing: a visitor who followed one of these is
# looking for Glamified Systems, and the homepage is where that conversation
# can still happen.
/glamifiedsales           /                            301
/glamified-sales          /                            301
/glamifiedfleet           /                            301
/glamified-fleet          /                            301

# Custom software development was removed when the site became a single-product
# GlamifiedHR site. The page ranked and was linked, so it goes to the one
# service that remains rather than 404ing — a visitor who followed it wanted
# something built or run for them, and payroll outsourcing is still that
# conversation. Change this to /contact if the service never comes back.
/services/web-software-development    /services/payroll-outsourcing    301
/web-software-development             /services/payroll-outsourcing    301
/custom-systems                       /services/payroll-outsourcing    301
